# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_ts_named_import_barrel.py" "TS NAMED-IMPORT BARREL RECALL GATE: PASS" "ts named-import barrel recall" "ts/js named-import -> barrel re-export recall: a barrel src/feat.ts re-exports { widget } from ./feat/widget.ts and a consumer imports { widget } from 'pkg/feat' — the consumer's REAL dependency is the IMPL file ./feat/widget.ts, but the extractor emitted ONLY the bare-module edge to the BARREL, so adjacency (which couples direct import pairs, not barrel hops) silently CLEARED the impl; FIX emits a name-qualified imports edge mod/<imported-name> per named specifier, the SAME shape Python's from-pkg-import-name already uses, so the resolver's EXISTING suffix/own-package probe reaches a submodule FILE named for the symbol; MEASURED on pmndrs/zustand: live dampened co-change recall 57.1 -> 71.4 pct (4/7 -> 5/7 GT pairs), raw import pairs 79 -> 91, every new live pair a REAL test->impl link, zero fabricated couplings (ky/zod unchanged, no over-firing); CONTENT-FREE (module path + imported identifier, never a body); PRECISION-SAFE — mod/nm resolves ONLY when a file carries that suffix, so an external { useState } from 'react' -> react/useState names no local file and stays inert; the IMPORTED name is read (not the local alias), and default/namespace imports emit no name-qualified edge; gate proves recall (barrel re-export resolves to the impl), precision (external named import + alias decoy + namespace import fabricate nothing), additivity (bare-module barrel edge unchanged), and a control that recall is load-bearing (a non-barrel does NOT reach the impl)" "ts/js named-import barrel recall: a re-exported symbol's real coupling is to its IMPL file, not the barrel — recall-safe and precision-preserving" 24
